{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.NewtonRealityInvariance","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.NewtonRealityInvariance","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Complex.Analytic"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.NewtonRealityInvariance.conjEquivariant_realPolynomial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.NewtonRealityInvariance.conjEquivariant_realPolynomial","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/NewtonRealityInvariance.lean#L105-L116","doc":"Concrete instance: a real-coefficient polynomial, evaluated over `ℂ`, is\nconjugation-equivariant — so the gluing polynomial and its derivative at real\nmeridian qualify, and the exclusion applies to the literal pole-seed Newton. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.NewtonRealityInvariance.real_seed_limit_ne_of_im_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.NewtonRealityInvariance.real_seed_limit_ne_of_im_ne","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/NewtonRealityInvariance.lean#L88-L103","doc":"**Real seeds cannot reach a non-real target.** If a Newton iteration with\nconjugation-equivariant data starts at a real seed (either sign) and\nconverges, its limit is real — in particular it is not any point with\nnon-zero imaginary part, such as the 4₁ cusp shape `e^{iπ/3}`\n(`Im = √3/2`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.NewtonRealityInvariance.limit_real","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.NewtonRealityInvariance.limit_real","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/NewtonRealityInvariance.lean#L77-L86","doc":"The limit of a convergent sequence of real (conjugation-fixed) complex\nnumbers is real: conjugation is continuous, so both `conj ∘ u` and `u` tend\nto `conj L` and `L`, and they are equal. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.NewtonRealityInvariance.iterate_real","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.NewtonRealityInvariance.iterate_real","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/NewtonRealityInvariance.lean#L65-L75","doc":"All Newton iterates of a real seed are real (conjugation-fixed). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.NewtonRealityInvariance.conjEquivariant_maps_real","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.NewtonRealityInvariance.conjEquivariant_maps_real","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/NewtonRealityInvariance.lean#L60-L63","doc":"A conjugation-equivariant map sends real points to real points. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.NewtonRealityInvariance.conjEquivariant_newtonStep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.NewtonRealityInvariance.conjEquivariant_newtonStep","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/NewtonRealityInvariance.lean#L53-L58","doc":"The Newton step of conjugation-equivariant maps is conjugation-equivariant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.NewtonRealityInvariance.newtonStep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.NewtonRealityInvariance.newtonStep","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/NewtonRealityInvariance.lean#L48-L51","doc":"The Newton step `z ↦ z − f z / g z` (with `g` the derivative in the\nintended reading — kept abstract; division by zero is junk-total as usual). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.NewtonRealityInvariance.ConjEquivariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.NewtonRealityInvariance.ConjEquivariant","kind":"def","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/NewtonRealityInvariance.lean#L43-L46","doc":"A map `ℂ → ℂ` that commutes with complex conjugation. Real-coefficient\npolynomials and their ratios satisfy this. ","signatureChunk":0}]}